A question for the user inside a plan: the user wants settings read from a
file and to choose the format before any code is written. The agent plans
the work, asks the question (an Ask in mem), and ends its turn without
writing the loader. The answer comes in the same conversation; the agent
records it, writes the loader in that format and closes the plan.

-- project/go.mod --
module app

go 1.22
-- project/main.go --
// Command app prints its settings.
package main

import "fmt"

// Settings are the app's settings.
type Settings struct {
	Name string
	Port int
}

func main() {
	s := Settings{Name: "app", Port: 8080}
	fmt.Printf("%s on %d\n", s.Name, s.Port)
}
-- prompt --
I want the settings in main.go read from a file instead of hard-coded, with a test for the loader. Plan it as todos in mem, but before you write any code, ask me which file format to use: I haven't decided between TOML and JSON.
-- prompt --
JSON, with the standard library only. Go ahead.
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
turn 1 tool edit == 0
turn 1 tool write == 0
answer 1 matches (?i)json
answer 1 matches (?i)toml
cmd go test ./...
cmd grep -rq 'encoding/json' --include='*.go' .
cmd ! grep -rqi toml --include='*.go' .
vm-dump contains json
mem-count open == 0
